         "for epoch in range(epochs):\n    preds = model(X_train)          # forward pass\n    loss = cross_entropy(preds, y)  # scorecard\n    loss.backward()                 # gradients: which way is down?\n    optimizer.step()                # take the step\n    optimizer.zero_grad()           # reset for next batch",
         "Each epoch: predict, score with the loss, compute gradients (the direction of steepest descent), step the weights, reset gradients. Watch the loss curve: if it explodes to NaN, the learning rate is too high; if it barely moves after epochs, it is too low or the features need scaling. This loop is the engine inside every neural network trainer.",
